# Line endings are a deployment concern here, not a style one.
#
# The repo is edited on Windows and runs on Linux. A shell script committed with
# CRLF fails on the VPS as `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` — which names
# neither the file nor the real problem — and a systemd unit with CRLF is parsed
# with a trailing \r inside every value, so ExecStart points at a path that does
# not exist. Both depend on whoever committed having core.autocrlf set the right
# way, which is not something to leave to chance.

* text=auto

*.sh text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
